m step by step. Give your final answer in \\boxed{...}.\n\nSimplify $(2+3i)(1-2i)$.","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"b3188db8b06cb50f916637f93358e0d7fbe3471cf20c658f6557d8367794b9e5"},"seconds":9.101369619369507,"seed":875451996031054798,"stop":"eos","text":"To simplify the expression \\((2+3i)(1-2i)\\), we will use the distributive property, also known as the FOIL method for binomials (First, Outer, Inner, Last). Let's break it down step by step.\n\n1. **First**: Multiply the first terms in each binomial.\n   \\[\n   2 \\cdot 1 = 2\n   \\]\n\n2. **Outer**: Multiply the outer terms in the product.\n   \\[\n   2 \\cdot (-2i) = -4i\n   \\]\n\n3. **Inner**: Multiply the inner terms in the product.\n   \\[\n   3i \\cdot 1 = 3i\n   \\]\n\n4. **Last**: Multiply the last terms in each binomial.\n   \\[\n   3i \\cdot (-2i) = -6i^2\n   \\]\n\nNow, we combine all these products:\n\\[\n2 + (-4i) + 3i + (-6i^2)\n\\]\n\nNext, we simplify by combining like terms and using the fact that \\(i^2 = -1\\):\n\\[\n2 - 4i + 3i - 6i^2\n\\]\n\nCombine the real parts and the imaginary parts:\n\\[\n2 - i - 6i^2\n\\]\n\nSubstitute \\(i^2 = -1\\):\n\\[\n2 - i - 6(-1)\n\\]\n\nSimplify the expression:\n\\[\n2 - i + 6\n\\]\n\nCombine the real parts:\n\\[\n8 - i\n\\]\n\nThus, the simplified form of \\((2+3i)(1-2i)\\) is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{8 - i}\n\\]"},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{8 - i}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true},"id":"algebra:949"}
